      'Pandit Vishnu Narayan Bhatkhande subsequently designated Bilawal as the primary Shuddha Thaat in his ten-Thaat system. In concert practice, two closely related forms exist: Devgiri/Shuddha Bilawal (which uses strictly the seven Shuddha swaras) and Alhaiya Bilawal (the universally performed concert form, which omits Madhyam in the primary ascending sweep `G P D N S\'` and introduces a delicate, ornamental touch of Komal Nishad `n` tucked inside descending Dhaivat phrases: `S\' N D, n D P`).',
